# The rotation algebra so(4) of four-dimensional space, the symmetry algebra of the mesh, modeled by the kernel as the
# direct sum of two copies of su(2). The great fact of dimension four is that so(4) SPLITS: so(4) = su(2) + su(2), the
# self-dual and anti-self-dual parts, and the two factors COMMUTE. This split is exactly the two spinor classes of the
# 24-cell (the D4 triality seen in the root system), the reason four-space carries free spin. This file builds an element
# of so(4) as a pair of su(2) elements and reuses the proven su(2) bracket componentwise, so the bracket is the direct
# sum. It then PROVES the defining law: a pure left rotation and a pure right rotation always commute.

load @term/seed/algebra/lie/su2
  find elem
  find bracket

# A rotor: an element of so(4), a left su(2) part and a right su(2) part. The whole algebra is the direct sum of the two.
form rotor
  case pair
    link left, like elem
    link right, like elem

# The so(4) bracket, the direct sum of the two su(2) brackets: bracket the left parts and the right parts independently.
# Because the parts never mix, the two su(2) factors are automatically independent subalgebras.
task so4-bracket
  take a, like rotor
  take b, like rotor
  like rotor
  fork case, read a
    case pair
      link left-a
      link right-a
      fork case, read b
        case pair
          link left-b
          link right-b
          send back
            make pair
              bind left
                call bracket
                  read left-a
                  read left-b
              bind right
                call bracket
                  read right-a
                  read right-b

# Lift a left su(2) element into so(4): a pure left rotation, with the right part at rest.
task pure-left
  take x, like elem
  like rotor
  send back
    make pair
      bind left
        read x
      bind right
        make zero

# Lift a right su(2) element into so(4): a pure right rotation, with the left part at rest.
task pure-right
  take x, like elem
  like rotor
  send back
    make pair
      bind left
        make zero
      bind right
        read x

# THE TWO FACTORS COMMUTE: the bracket of a pure left rotation and a pure right rotation is zero, for every pair of su(2)
# elements. so4-bracket (pure-left a) (pure-right b) = the zero rotor. This is the heart of so(4) = su(2) + su(2): the
# self-dual and anti-self-dual rotations are independent, which is why four-space carries two separate spins.
rule left-and-right-commute
  mark a, like elem
  mark b, like elem
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call so4-bracket
        call pure-left
          read a
        call pure-right
          read b
      make pair
        bind left
          make zero
        bind right
          make zero
  fold a, b

# The bracket is also ALTERNATING in each factor (a rotor brackets to zero with itself), inherited directly from the two
# su(2) alternating laws proved in su2.tree, since the so(4) bracket is their componentwise direct sum.

# A PURE LEFT ROTATION CLOSES IN THE LEFT FACTOR: the bracket of two pure left rotations is again a pure left rotation,
# its right part at rest. so4-bracket (pure-left a) (pure-left b) has right part zero, for every a and b. The left su(2)
# is a genuine subalgebra, never leaking into the right factor.
rule left-factor-is-closed
  mark a, like elem
  mark b, like elem
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call so4-bracket
        call pure-left
          read a
        call pure-left
          read b
      make pair
        bind left
          call bracket
            read a
            read b
        bind right
          make zero
  calm hold
